,"output_tokens":6144,"requests":10}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"a62ff1c9c6f92aee69c5ca33067a74472231974eae6c48b59add1cf560b8f932"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":236299,"output_tokens":5289,"requests":8}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Normalize case when testing never-counted membership (lowercase the _DIRTY_LINE_SPECS-derived kinds so they match the lowercased item['kind']), and make the G6 drift-guard assert against the lowercased set actually used at the stamping site so the case-fold seam is covered.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan defines `_NEVER_COUNTED_TRACKER_DIRTY_KINDS = {kind for (_, kind, _, counted) in _DIRTY_LINE_SPECS if not counted}`","_DIRTY_LINE_SPECS kinds are UPPERCASE: fsck_tracker_health.py lines 256-277 ('TRACKER_DIRTY_TMP_EVENT')","_transform_json lowercases before building the item: fsck.py line 127 `kind, rest = m.group(1).lower(), m.group(2)`","So `'tracker_dirty_tmp_event' not in {'TRACKER_DIRTY_TMP_EVENT'}` is always True → counted=True, re-inflating issue_count for the very kind the plan fixes","The step-7 drift guard as specified compares the derived set to `{kind for _DIRTY_LINE_SPECS if not counted}` (uppercase both sides) → it passes and does NOT catch the case mismatch"],"finding":"The plan's derived never-counted tracker-dirty kind set is uppercase (from _DIRTY_LINE_SPECS) but is matched against lowercased item['kind'], so the tmp-event kind is never recognized as never-counted and would be wrongly stamped counted=True.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f16295bbaa4eff049","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation plan, step 1 (_transform_json kind-set + `counted = kind not in _NEVER_COUNTED_KINDS`) and step 7 drift guard","norm_id":"nd751645f4f9340b5","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A store with an orphaned .tmp-event-* staging file: TRACKER_DIRTY_TMP_EVENT is emitted (is_issue=False, not in _scan's tally), but JSON issue_count would still count it → disagrees with exit code, the exact bug"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Derive with `.lower()`: `_NEVER_COUNTED_TRACKER_DIRTY_KINDS = {kind.lower() for (_, kind, _, counted) in _DIRTY_LINE_SPECS if not counted}` (and likewise wherever the union is built), and have the drift-guard test compare against the same lowercased set the stamping uses.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Close the scan-kind drift gap: either derive _NEVER_COUNTED_SCAN_KINDS from the per-site is_issue flags (as done for tracker-dirty), or add a drift-guard test that enumerates ALL emitted scan/health kinds and asserts every is_issue=False one is in the constant (not merely a fixture-bound behavioural invariant).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6","T5e"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3544,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'The three scan/health kinds decided by an inline is_issue=False are an explicit _NEVER_COUNTED_SCAN_KINDS = {\"push_pending\", \"status_fork_resolved\", \"warn\"}; each production site carries a pointer comment back to the constant.'","'a behavioural invariant that the counted subset equals the exit-code tally across a payload mixing every never-counted kind — so a new is_issue=False kind that forgets the constant fails a test'","ABSENCE: the behavioural invariant proves nothing about a kind not present in the fixture payload, so the claim 'a new is_issue=False kind ... fails a test' does not hold for the scan-kind literal side"],"finding":"The drift-guard (step 7) fully closes drift for the tracker-dirty portion (derived from _DIRTY_LINE_SPECS), but the three inline scan/health kinds remain a hand-maintained literal (_NEVER_COUNTED_SCAN_KINDS). The only guard for a NEW is_issue=False scan kind is the behavioural invariant 'counted subset equals exit-code tally across a payload mixing every never-counted kind' — which only exercises kinds already present in the test fixture, so a future inline is_issue=False scan kind that forgets the constant would silently re-inflate issue_count and not fail any test.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa3d4131a26024b2e","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Step 7 (Drift guard) / Step 1 (_NEVER_COUNTED_SCAN_KINDS)","norm_id":"n5a32c323901b104a","priority":0.5956,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future contributor adds a new inline is_issue=False scan finding without adding it to _NEVER_COUNTED_SCAN_KINDS; JSON issue_count counts it while the exit code does not — the exact bug this plan fixes silently returns"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a test that iterates the actual is_issue=False emission sites (or a registry) and asserts each corresponding JSON kind is in _NEVER_COUNTED_KINDS, so a newly-added inline is_issue=False scan kind fails the guard regardless of whether it appears in the mixed-store fixture.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate tests/unit/test_unsigned_env_fsck_heldout.py:128 as a site pinning the old `issue_count == len(issues)` equivalence and confirm (or update) that its counted-only payload keeps the assertion valid under the redefinition.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4578,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan step 6 enumerates only test_fsck_structured_326f.py, test_fsck_ensures.py, test_repair_pause_ownership_heldout.py, and the new test_fsck_issue_count_29c3.py","Consumer assessment: 'No external or CI consumer reads issue_count (only rebar's own tests)'","test_unsigned_env_fsck_heldout.py:128: `assert payload[\"issue_count\"] == len(payload[\"issues\"]) >= 1` — a second in-repo site encoding the old equivalence, unlisted in the plan"],"finding":"The plan's test